        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cad626e8-e595-5298-bc6d-625ac19af876",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Harry Emerson Fosdick\n- Organizations: First Presbyterian Church, Riverside Church\n- Places: New York City, Manhattan, West Village, Morningside Heights, Upper Manhattan\n- Roles: pastor\n\nFacts:\n- Harry Emerson Fosdick was born on May 24, 1878, and he was an American pastor.\n- Harry Emerson Fosdick, although a Baptist, was called to serve as pastor at First Presbyterian Church in Manhattan's West Village in New York City.\n- Harry Emerson Fosdick later served as pastor at the historic inter-denominational Riverside Church in Morningside Heights, Manhattan.\n- Riverside Church is a Christian church in Morningside Heights, Upper Manhattan, New York City.\n- Riverside Church opened its doors on October 5, 1930.\n- Harry Emerson Fosdick died on October 5, 1969.",
